沃靠，干货又来了！！这真得关注一下。

@xitang_ai 西堂老师在AI短剧方面的研究，真是太深刻了，之前还开源了他们辛苦搞了几年的所有关于AI做视频的方法知识库，我看了下，全部都是干货内容。

如今这篇内容，又把短剧和可灵的使用方法全部公开了，提示词也分享了，牛逼，AI短剧界的赛博菩萨啊。

Have been doing lots of these prompts lately. This one was done for poets. 

2x2 grid, 16:9, do this for 4 GOAT poets: INPUT: $ WORD, $ STROKE_STYLE, $ FORMAT
// Compute grapheme skeleton for each letter and a continuity potential Φ over the word sequence.
Φ = continuous_stroke_potential($ WORD)   // keeps all strokes in one connected field
F = ∇Φ        // stroke direction from first letter to last
Curl = ∇×Φ    // rotational motion for middle morph and final trail
Div = ∇·F     // density of ink/smoke/neon/ribbon folds

// P2 Legibility:
// For each letter_i, enforce L_i = legibility(letter_i) ≥ τ by preserving negative space and stroke topology.
// Use a penalty that pushes ∇Φ away from filling counters.

// P3 Morph gradient:
// Let s ∈ [0,1] be position along the word. Define a warping field W(s):
//   s ∈ [0.0,0.3] -> letters grounded, regular readable base.
//   s ∈ [0.3,0.75] -> strokes morph into BODY_ARCHETYPE; pose expresses ACTIVITY.
//   s ∈ [0.75,1.0] -> strokes extend into trail / limb / fabric / energy echo.

// P1 Single stroke language: body emerges from letter strokes only.
// P5 Format: canvas dimensions selected; word flows edge-to-edge, negative space intact.

// Honest Stroke:
if $ STROKE_STYLE == "ink": width = pressure_map(∇Φ); texture = dry_brush_noise.
if "neon": emissive = glow_falloff(stroke_mask).
if "smoke": diffusion = blur(stroke_field, time).
if "wire": uniform continuous line, no taper.
if "ribbon": normal_fold = cross(∇Φ, Curl).
if "silk": drape = cloth_sim(stroke_field).
if "charcoal": grain = charcoal_texture(stroke_mask).

Render one image, 8K.

This prompt was made for another topic but I used it for famous musicians. 

Prompt: 2x2 grid, 16:9, do this for 4 GOAT musicians     INPUT: $ subject
// Infer all symbolic layers from the subjects's life and work. 
CORE = infer_signature_phenomenon($ subjects)
RELICS = infer_signature_relics($ subjects)
EQS = infer_key_equations($ subjects)
MAT = infer_person_material($ subjects)
INTERIOR = infer_interior_world($ subjects)
DUALITY = infer_core_duality($ subjects)
LIFE = infer_inhabitants($ subjects)
MOTION = infer_kinetic_behavior($ subjects)
PARTS = infer_exploded_parts($ subjects)
CHAIN = infer_scale_chain($ subjects)
CYCLE = infer_temporal_cycle($ subjects)
THIRD = infer_conceptual_third($ subjects)
VESSEL = infer_sacred_vessel($ subjects)

// Build a 10-layer potential field Φ over the diorama.
Φ = Σ w_i * layer_potential(i)   // each inheritance layer adds energy
F = ∇Φ       // main structural lines, guide-wires for exploded parts
Curl = ∇×Φ   // kinetic orbits, accretion swirls, automaton paths
Div = ∇·F    // density of annotations, labels, inhabitant clusters

// RUNG 1: Isometric Monument
//   Headline: $ subjects's name as huge 3D letters cut from MAT. 
//   Core phenomenon at center, glowing.
//   Relics instead of portrait unless mode=present.
//   Equations on blackboards/plaques.
//   Quote on brass base plaque.
// RUNG 2: Cutaway Reliquary
//   Clean section plane through plinth or phenomenon reveals INTERIOR.
// RUNG 3: Split-State Diorama
//   Bisect whole scene into two materials for DUALITY.
// RUNG 4: Inhabited Micro-World
//   Tiny LIFE in mid-action.
// RUNG 5: Kinetic Instrument
//   MOTION as working mechanism, orbit trails/motion blur.
// RUNG 6: Exploded Codex
//   PARTS separated with gold guide-lines and labels.
// RUNG 7: Fractal Scale-Jump
//   CHAIN nested: zoom reveals smaller dioramas.
// RUNG 8: Living Cosmos
//   CYCLE pulse, drifting light, active/resting states.
// RUNG 9: Multistable Monument
//   Three readings: name / phenomenon / THIRD.
// RUNG 10: Universe-in-a-Box
//   VESSEL binds all layers into one holdable relic.

Render: tilt-shift miniature, soft cinematic light, seamless white background, 8K, all equations legible.
